Chapter: KeyTabSingle
  cites UI chapter Focus
  cites UI chapter KeyInput

 Measured 2026-07-28 against seed 759D3E0F, before the duplicate was
 removed: here 9, keyinput 1048579, named no, verdict DISAGREE. The 9 was a
 leftover ASCII tab in `UI Focus` that no caller ever read and that
 `poll-key` cannot produce, so a Tab test written against it would have been
 dead code that looked correct.

Section: Body

  tab-here : Integer = key-tab

  tab-in-keyinput : Integer = scancode-to-keycode 15

  enter-here : Integer = key-enter

  enter-in-keyinput : Integer = scancode-to-keycode 28

  verdict : Integer, Integer -> Text
  verdict (a) (b) = if a == b then "AGREE" else "DISAGREE"

  yes-no : Boolean -> Text
  yes-no (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("tab here=" & show tab-here)
    print-line-uni ("tab keyinput=" & show tab-in-keyinput)
    print-line-uni ("tab named=" & yes-no (key-is-named tab-here))
    print-line-uni ("tab verdict=" & verdict tab-here tab-in-keyinput)
    print-line-uni ("enter verdict=" & verdict enter-here enter-in-keyinput)
    print-line-uni ("enter named=" & yes-no (key-is-named enter-here))
  end

